{"lines":[{"x":0.82089539440285786,"c":1,"w":0.082471752166747958,"h":0.016833319025247651,"y":0.038182038550731434,"t":"Reading"},{"c":1,"t":"As important as Wegener's work on continental drift has turned out to be, it was largely","w":0.81747568766276035,"h":0.019021227352344461,"y":0.087209302365756747,"x":0.067961181047260677},{"h":0.0203347749799212,"y":0.10719600592540124,"t":"a sideline to his interest in atmospheric physics, geophysics, and paleoclimatology,","w":0.78650990804036469,"c":1,"x":0.067905433300019899},{"w":0.78850077311197908,"y":0.12546593316688126,"c":1,"x":0.067886730970723577,"h":0.019839344440590878,"t":"and thus I have been at great pains to put Wegener's work on continental drift in the"},{"c":1,"y":0.14259381307491747,"w":0.81960332234700506,"t":"larger context of his other scientific work, and in the even larger context of atmospheric","x":0.065916937543067225,"h":0.021801974097516275},{"t":"sciences in his lifetime. This is a 'continental drift book' only to the extent that Wegener","y":0.16144985725134731,"x":0.067889561062899784,"h":0.020814471378504673,"w":0.81567362467447913,"c":1},{"y":0.18138381242712831,"w":0.80403391520182288,"h":0.020181802054431985,"c":1,"x":0.058200348804864653,"t":"was interested in that topic and later became famous for it. My treatment of his other"},{"t":"scientific work is no less detailed, though I certainly have devoted more attention","h":0.017591284517187167,"c":1,"x":0.067961169154204693,"w":0.75728154500325517,"y":0.2020348836078556},{"h":0.019099499949042253,"c":1,"t":"to the reception of his ideas on continental displacement, as they were much more","x":0.065963401195729715,"y":0.21931529433622232,"w":0.77681050618489578},{"c":1,"h":0.018442639977761188,"x":0.067858540344078802,"y":0.23741937625975218,"t":"controversial than his other work.","w":0.3167438252766927},{"y":0.27601246120890299,"t":"Readers interested in the specific detail of Wegener's career will see that he often","h":0.01759219006214563,"c":1,"x":0.069902905361450399,"w":0.76699030558268233},{"w":0.78252426147460941,"c":1,"x":0.067961170144505451,"y":0.29501557643213205,"h":0.017484423676012328,"t":"stopped pursuing a given line of investigation (sometimes for years on end), only to"},{"w":0.77101003011067715,"c":1,"y":0.31211981862606986,"h":0.019987813408872457,"t":"pick it up later. I have tried to provide guideposts to his rapidly shifting interests by","x":0.065948821678954814},{"y":0.33139534872271614,"x":0.067961157863229857,"t":"characterizing different phases of his life as careers in different sciences, which is","c":1,"w":0.76699030558268233,"h":0.017514308442208026},{"w":0.79046778361002623,"c":1,"t":"reflected in the titles of the chapters. Thus, the index should be a sufficient guide for","y":0.34873446824644816,"h":0.021877512233650864,"x":0.067877069113415678},{"w":0.82524271647135428,"x":0.067961166016558827,"t":"those interested in a particular aspect of Wegener's life but perhaps not all of it. My own","c":1,"h":0.01746902881753043,"y":0.36915887826546467},{"t":"feeling, however, is that the parts do not make as much sense on their own as do all of","h":0.020977500368872914,"c":1,"y":0.38659300164624788,"w":0.81958017985026044,"x":0.065963181323340142},{"y":0.40251126510071666,"t":"his activities taken together. In this respect I urge readers to try to experience Wegener's","c":1,"x":0.06784873715742909,"w":0.83520192464192711,"h":0.024655878655264307},{"w":0.75741928100585931,"y":0.4242802247070252,"x":0.065968740141281235,"h":0.021669462685273144,"t":"life as he lived it, with all the interruptions, changes of mind, and renewed efforts","c":1},{"h":0.016199376947040545,"w":0.12427185058593751,"c":1,"y":0.44610591897597329,"t":"this entailed.","x":0.067961161982112134},{"h":0.019003115264797477,"y":0.48099688445401501,"c":1,"x":0.069902918525802701,"w":0.75145629882812504,"t":"Wegener left behind a few published works but, as was standard practice, these"},{"t":"reported the results of his work - not the journey he took to reach that point. Only a","w":0.78266179402669267,"h":0.020327103992117568,"x":0.067891555378619628,"c":1,"y":0.49838447398536456},{"t":"tew hundred of the many thousands of letters he wrote and received in his lifetime","w":0.77297663370768233,"h":0.018878355650144285,"x":0.067871924412470239,"y":0.5170422512982733,"c":1},{"w":0.7477140808105468,"t":"have survived and he didn't keep notebooks or diaries that recorded his life and","y":0.53604537377679318,"x":0.069834069958923897,"h":0.01868078285288588,"c":1},{"t":"activities. He was not active (with a few exceptions) in scientific societies, and did not","w":0.80194173177083328,"h":0.017534231619671492,"x":0.069902920699509721,"y":0.55514018708653601,"c":1},{"t":"seek to find influence or advance his ideas through professional contacts and politics,","x":0.069902902959243632,"h":0.017460878318715345,"y":0.57412790686242199,"w":0.80388351440429695,"c":1},{"h":0.017568644704848424,"c":1,"x":0.069902908895160279,"w":0.75533981323242183,"t":"spending most of his time at home in his study reading and writing, or in the field","y":0.59302325569942438},{"y":0.61337209311023522,"x":0.069902913500055827,"t":"collecting observations.","w":0.22524271647135413,"h":0.015988371899566256,"c":1},{"x":0.0699029197979011,"h":0.019033905575951304,"w":0.83300969441731776,"c":1,"t":"Some famous scientists, such as Newton, Darwin, and Einstein, left mountains of written","y":0.64825581422474876},{"c":1,"x":0.069815208360252443,"t":"material behind, hundreds of notebooks and letters numbering in the tens of thousands.","y":0.66474459081904702,"w":0.82539677937825506,"h":0.022192575329932129},{"t":"Others, like Michael Faraday, left extensive journals of their thoughts and speculations,","x":0.06986356017780708,"y":0.68483217585649625,"w":0.81754562377929685,"h":0.020250049484110355,"c":1},{"w":0.81165049235026054,"t":"parallel to their scientific notebooks. The more such material a scientist leaves behind,","x":0.069902909084327405,"y":0.70342679135766273,"h":0.017503441308517664,"c":1},{"t":"the better chance a biographer has of forming an accurate picture of how a scientist's","x":0.069902920498930141,"c":1,"w":0.80194173177083339,"h":0.017491668629869173,"y":0.72238372081586066},{"x":0.066019423054818227,"t":"ideas took shape and evolved.","y":0.74267912751310572,"w":0.29514561971028647,"h":0.016041802617248413,"c":1},{"h":0.020249915197259605,"c":1,"t":"I am firmly of the opinion that most of us, Wegener included, are not in any real sense","w":0.80785858154296886,"y":0.77746808333621942,"x":0.067922908259238468},{"x":0.069902928969884592,"y":0.79651162794715213,"h":0.0188953482844747,"t":"the authors of our own lives. We plan, think, and act, often with apparent freedom,","w":0.77281550089518225,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.81526479775294458,"t":"but most of the time our lives 'happen to us', and we only retrospectively turn this","w":0.76116505940755208,"x":0.069902907147250531,"h":0.017584039563330545},{"w":0.80776697794596342,"t":"happenstance into a coherent narrative of fulfilled intentions. This book, therefore, is a","y":0.83426791276548229,"h":0.019003115264797477,"c":1,"x":0.06990291888160613},{"c":1,"x":0.069801960635643728,"h":0.021427722586278231,"w":0.81185745239257812,"y":0.85151805912612089,"t":"story both of the life and scientific work that Alfred Wegener planned and intended and"},{"h":0.017572266884682053,"t":"of the life and scientific work that actually 'happened to him'. These are, as I think you","x":0.069902902985589516,"y":0.87196261694197685,"w":0.80388351440429684,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"will soon see, not always the same thing.","w":0.39050226847330738,"x":0.069780465499616889,"h":0.019379067346685708,"y":0.89125312715732197},{"t":"* Paleoclimatology - The study of past climates","y":0.93014644428045512,"x":0.069664382700055899,"w":0.28584513346354168,"h":0.015276975423747507,"c":1},{"h":0.015988371899566256,"c":1,"w":0.029126211802164681,"x":0.87961165127529306,"t":"93","y":0.95348837212313353}],"w":2400,"h":3209}